xpilot-ref patch 0005: optional per-tick trace of balls, asteroids, wreckage,
race progress, treasures and targets, and of the random generator.

This patch modifies XPilot 4.5.5 (GPL-2.0-or-later, Copyright (C) 1991-2010
by Bjoern Stabell, Ken Ronny Schouten, Bert Gijsbers, Dick Balaska et al.).
It is a derivative work distributed under the same license.

Why: to compare the reimplementation's game modes (ball connector physics,
asteroid motion and placement, race timing and respawn, treasure and target
state) numerically against the original server, replaying its random stream.
Applies on top of patches 0002, 0003 and 0004.  Adds Trace_modes() to
src/server/server.c, called right after Trace_objects(), and a randomMT()
call counter with a state dump to src/common/randommt.c.  It is inert unless
the environment variable XPILOT_TRACE_MODES is set (the counter only counts).
Game logic is unchanged.

--- a/src/common/randommt.c
+++ b/src/common/randommt.c
@@ -159,10 +159,36 @@
 }
 
 
+#include <stdio.h>
+
+/*
+ * xpilot-ref trace hooks (not part of upstream XPilot 4.5.5): a count of
+ * randomMT() calls and a dump of the generator state, so a reimplementation
+ * can replay this server's random stream.  Game logic is unchanged.
+ */
+static unsigned long	trace_mt_draws;
+
+unsigned long Trace_MT_draws(void)
+{
+    return trace_mt_draws;
+}
+
+void Trace_MT_dump(FILE *fp)
+{
+    int i;
+
+    fprintf(fp, " %lu %d %d", trace_mt_draws, left,
+	    next != NULL ? (int)(next - state) : 0);
+    for (i = 0; i <= N; i++) {
+	fprintf(fp, " %u", (unsigned) state[i]);
+    }
+}
+
 unsigned int randomMT(void)
 {
     uint32 y;
 
+    trace_mt_draws++;
     if (--left < 0)
 	return (reloadMT());
 
